---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import MedicalDisclaimer from '../components/MedicalDisclaimer.astro';
import FormattedDate from '../components/FormattedDate.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import authorPhoto from '../assets/denis-ethier.png';
import { sortPostsDescending } from '../utils/postUtils';

const rawPosts = await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
// Show posts relevant for medical practitioners, neurologists, ENTs, and primary care
const doctorPosts = sortPostsDescending(rawPosts).filter(post => {
	const tags = post.data.tags || [];
	return tags.includes('clinician') || tags.includes('both');
});
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead 
			title="For Doctors | Decoding The Burn" 
			description="How neurologists, ENTs, and physicians can leverage longitudinal patient datasets and neuropathic phenotyping in Burning Mouth Syndrome." 
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<!-- Hero Section Following Homepage Model -->
			<section class="hero-centered-wrapper">
				<div class="hero-centered-header">
					<MedicalDisclaimer />
					<h1 class="hero-centered-title">
						How Doctors Can Use This&nbsp;Site
					</h1>
					<p class="hero-centered-subtitle">
						When patients suffer from severe neuropathic burning and blood panels return normal, medicine needs new models.
						Here is how dense, longitudinal biometric and dietary latency tracking uncovers neuropathic&nbsp;pathways.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Video on Top -->
				<div class="hero-video-centered">
					<div class="video-placeholder-wrapper" style="cursor: default;">
						<Image 
							src={authorPhoto} 
							alt="Denis Ethier - BMS Medical Orientation Video" 
							class="video-placeholder-img" 
							width={1400} 
							height={788} 
						/>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Message to Doctors Card Under Video -->
				<article class="personal-story-section">
					<h2 class="story-heading">My Experience &amp; A Message to Medical Specialists</h2>
					<div class="story-lead">
						<p class="story-paragraph">
							Over three agonizing years of Burning Mouth Syndrome, I consulted five medical specialists, including ENTs, 
							neurologists, and internal medicine physicians. I was prescribed tricyclic antidepressants, gabapentinoids, 
							and oral rinses. While these medications are standard of care, they did not address the underlying neuro-inflammatory 
							firing mechanisms.
						</p>
						<p class="story-paragraph">
							As an engineer and researcher, I approached my diagnosis through systems biology and signal processing. 
							What emerged was a clear understanding of <strong>small-fiber neuropathy, central sensitization, and delayed 
							gastrointestinal-mucosal biochemical cascades (the 72-hour latency window)</strong>.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="story-body-grid">
						<div class="story-card">
							<div class="story-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
								<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
									<path d="M22 12h-4l-3 9L9 3l-3 9H2"></path>
								</svg>
							</div>
							<h3 class="story-card-title">1. Small-Fiber Neuropathy &amp; Trigeminal Signaling</h3>
							<p class="story-card-text">
								BMS frequently represents peripheral small-fiber sensory neuropathy of the chorda tympani and lingual nerve. 
								Treating it strictly as idiopathic often misses the mechanical-chemical triggers in the oral environment.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="story-card">
							<div class="story-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
								<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
									<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
									<polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"></polyline>
								</svg>
							</div>
							<h3 class="story-card-title">2. The 72-Hour Latency Window</h3>
							<p class="story-card-text">
								Neuro-inflammatory cascades often have multi-day latency. Tracking dietary challenges across a 72-hour timeline 
								reveals distinct smoldering and flare phases that traditional single-day recall fails to detect.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="story-card">
							<div class="story-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
								<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
									<path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"></path>
									<polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"></polyline>
									<line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"></line>
									<line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"></line>
									<polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"></polyline>
								</svg>
							</div>
							<h3 class="story-card-title">3. Beyond Anti-Depressants</h3>
							<p class="story-card-text">
								When bloodwork and biopsies return normal, patients are frequently told their symptoms are psychogenic. 
								Structured elimination diets and mechanical hardware remediation offer non-pharmacological avenues for symptom reduction.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Direct Collaboration CTA -->
					<div class="collab-cta-box">
						<h3 class="collab-cta-title">Are you a physician or medical researcher studying BMS?</h3>
						<p class="collab-cta-text">
							I am actively partnering with neurologists, ENTs, and oral medicine researchers to share open time-series patient 
							datasets and discuss clinical hypotheses on the podcast.
						</p>
						<div class="collab-cta-actions">
							<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Contact Me</a>
							<a href="/podcast/professional-guide" class="btn btn-secondary">Physician Guest Guide</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- Medical Articles Section -->
				<section class="patient-articles-section">
					<div class="section-heading-wrapper">
						<h2 class="section-title">Medical &amp; Neurological Research Articles</h2>
						<p class="section-subtitle">
							In-depth analysis of neurological pathways, medical literature, systemic inflammation, and patient trial protocols.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="articles-grid">
						{doctorPosts.map((post) => (
							<article class="article-card">
								<a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`} class="article-card-link">
									{post.data.heroImage && (
										<div class="article-image-wrapper">
											<img 
												src={post.data.heroImage} 
												alt={post.data.title} 
												class="article-image" 
												loading="lazy"
											/>
										</div>
									)}
									<div class="article-content">
										<div class="article-meta">
											<span class="article-category">{post.data.category || 'Medical'}</span>
											<span class="meta-separator">•</span>
											<span class="article-date"><FormattedDate date={post.data.pubDate} /></span>
										</div>
										<h3 class="article-title">{post.data.title}</h3>
										<p class="article-desc">{post.data.description}</p>
									</div>
								</a>
							</article>
						))}
					</div>
				</section>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.hero-centered-wrapper {
		max-width: 1100px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
	}

	.hero-centered-header {
		text-align: center;
		max-width: 780px;
		margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
	}

	.hero-centered-title {
		font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
		font-weight: 800;
		line-height: 1.15;
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin: 1.25rem 0 1rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.hero-centered-subtitle {
		font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin: 0;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.hero-video-centered {
		max-width: 900px;
		margin: 0 auto 3rem;
		border-radius: 20px;
		overflow: hidden;
		box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08));
		background: #000000;
	}

	.video-placeholder-wrapper {
		position: relative;
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
	}

	.video-placeholder-img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		opacity: 0.95;
	}

	.personal-story-section {
		background: var(--bg-card, #ffffff);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e2e8f0);
		border-radius: 24px;
		padding: 3rem 2.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 4rem;
		box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
	}

	.story-heading {
		font-size: 1.85rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
		text-align: center;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.story-lead {
		max-width: 800px;
		margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
	}

	.story-paragraph {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}

	.story-body-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	.story-card {
		background: #f8fafc;
		border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
		border-radius: 16px;
		padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem;
	}

	.story-card-icon {
		color: #991b1b;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.story-card-title {
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.story-card-text {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.collab-cta-box {
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e1136 0%, #0d081a 100%);
		border-radius: 18px;
		padding: 2.25rem 2rem;
		text-align: center;
		color: #ffffff;
		border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3);
	}

	.collab-cta-title {
		font-size: 1.35rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.collab-cta-text {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: #e2e8f0;
		max-width: 620px;
		margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.collab-cta-actions {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		justify-content: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}

	.patient-articles-section {
		margin-top: 3rem;
	}

	.section-heading-wrapper {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
	}

	.section-title {
		font-size: 2rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.section-subtitle {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		max-width: 600px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.articles-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.article-card {
		background: #ffffff;
		border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
		border-radius: 16px;
		overflow: hidden;
		transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
	}

	.article-card:hover {
		transform: translateY(-4px);
		box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
	}

	.article-card-link {
		text-decoration: none;
		color: inherit;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		height: 100%;
	}

	.article-image-wrapper {
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
		overflow: hidden;
		background: #f1f5f9;
	}

	.article-image {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	.article-content {
		padding: 1.5rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		flex: 1;
	}

	.article-meta {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: #64748b;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.article-category {
		font-weight: 700;
		color: #991b1b;
	}

	.article-title {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.3;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.article-desc {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin: 0;
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.personal-story-section {
			padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
		}
	}
</style>
